, 10.08, 6300, 7875, 1000. Note Q2/Q1: 12.6×1.6=20.16 ✓; 6.3×1.6=10.08 ✓. Q4/Q3: 6300×1.25=7875 ✓.\n\nNow build the JSON.\n\ncertificate:\n{\n  \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\",\n  \"scheme\": \"A\",\n  \"project_number\": \"3528374\",\n  \"page_total\": 12,\n  \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\",\n  \"date_issued\": \"2022-08-30\",\n  \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n}\n\nissuing_authority:\n{\n  \"name\": \"NMi Certin B.V.\",\n  \"address_lines\": [\"Thijsseweg 11\", \"2629 JA Delft\", \"The Netherlands\"],\n  \"person_responsible\": \"M.Ph.D. Schmidt\",\n  \"phone\": \"+31 88 636 2332\",\n  \"email\": \"certin@nmi.nl\",\n  \"website\": \"www.nmi.nl\",\n  \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n}\n\napplicants: [{\"name\": \"ABB Limited\", \"address_lines\": [\"Oldends Lane\", \"GL10 3TA Stonehouse\", \"United Kingdom\"]}]\n\nmanufacturers: same.\n\ncertified_type:\n{\n  \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n  \"type_designations\": [\"AquaMaster4 FEW4XY.Z\", \"FET4*\"],\n  \"description\": \"An electromagnetic water meter\"\n}\n\nmodel_family:\n{\n  \"family_name\": \"AquaMaster4\",\n  \"models\": [30 entries]\n}\n\nEach: {\"model_id\": \"DN40 class 1\", \"label\": \"DN40, accuracy class 1 (reduced bore, AC mains powered)\", \"attributes\": {\"nominal_size_dn\": 40, \"accuracy_class\": 1}}\n\nHmm label — keep simple: \"DN40 class 1 (reduced bore, AC mains powered)\". I'll do label: \"Reduced bore, AC mains powered\". Repeated. Or omit label. Schema: model_id, label, attributes. label optional-ish; I'll set label to null? \"include ONLY if cert covers >1 model variant\" — it does. label: I'll use \"Reduced bore – AC mains powered\". Fine.\n\nModel ids — let me choose \"DN40 class 1\" style.\n\nList:\nDN40 c1 (0.05,0.08,25,31.25,500)\nDN40 c2 (0.025,0.04,25,31.25,1000)\nDN50 c1 (0.08,0.128,40,50,500)\nDN50 c2 (0.04,0.064,40,50,1000)\nDN65 c1 (0.063,0.1008,63,78.75,1000)\nDN65 c2 (same)\nDN80 c1 (0.1,0.16,100,125,1000)\nDN80 c2 (same)\nDN100 c1 (0.32,0.512,160,200,500)\nDN100 c2 (0.16,0.256,160,200,1000)\nDN125 c1 (0.32,0.512,160,200,500)\nDN125 c2 (0.16,0.256,160,200,1000)\nDN150 c1 (0.4,0.64,400,500,1000)\nDN150 c2 (same)\nDN200 c1 (0.63,1.008,630,787.5,1000)\nDN200 c2 (same)\nDN250 c1 (2,3.2,1000,1250,500)\nDN250 c2 (1,1.6,1000,1250,1000)\nDN300 c1 (3.2,5.12,1600,2000,500)\nDN300 c2 (1.6,2.56,1600,2000,1000)\nDN350 c1 (3.2,5.12,1600,2000,500)\nDN350 c2 (1.6,2.56,1600,2000,1000)\nDN400 c1 (5,8,2500,3125,500)\nDN400 c2 (same)\nDN450 c1 (5,8,2500,3125,500)\nDN450 c2 (same)\nDN500 c1 (8,12.8,4000,5000,500)\nDN500 c2 (4,6.4,4000,5000,1000)\nDN600 c1 (12.6,20.16,6300,7875,500)\nDN600 c2 (6.3,10.08,6300,7875,1000)\n\ncharacteristics.model_level: 5 attributes × 30 values.\n\nLet me write them out.\n\nq1 values:\nDN40 c1 0.05; DN40 c2 0.025; DN50 c1 0.08; DN50 c2 0.04; DN65 c1 0.063; DN65 c2 0.063; DN80 c1 0.1; DN80 c2 0.1; DN100 c1 0.32; DN100 c2 0.16; DN125 c1 0.32; DN125 c2 0.16; DN150 c1 0.4; DN150 c2 0.4; DN200 c1 0.63; DN200 c2 0.63; DN250 c1 2; DN250 c2 1; DN300 c1 3.2; DN300 c2 1.6; DN350 c1 3.2; DN350 c2 1.6; DN400 c1 5; DN400 c2 5; DN450 c1 5; DN450 c2 5; DN500 c1 8; DN500 c2 4; DN600 c1 12.6; DN600 c2 6.3.\n\nq2 values:\n0.08, 0.04, 0.128, 0.064, 0.1008, 0.1008, 0.16, 0.16, 0.512, 0.256, 0.512, 0.256, 0.64, 0.64, 1.008, 1.008, 3.2, 1.6, 5.12, 2.56, 5.12, 2.56, 8, 8, 8, 8, 12.8, 6.4, 20.16, 10.08.\n\nq3: 25,25,40,40,63,63,100,100,160,160,160,160,400,400,630,630,1000,1000,1600,1600,1600,1600,2500,2500,2500,2500,4000,4000,6300,6300.\n\nq4: 31.25,31.25,50,50,78.75,78.75,125,125,200,200,200,200,500,500,787.5,787.5,1250,1250,2000,2000,2000,2000,3125,3125,3125,3125,5000,5000,7875,7875.\n\nq3_q1_ratio: 500,1000,500,1000,1000,1000,1000,1000,500,1000,500,1000,1000,1000,1000,1000,500,1000,500,1000,500,1000,500,500,500,500,500,1000,500,1000.\n\nmatrix_tables[0]:\nname: \"General characteristics of the family of instruments — reduced bore, AC mains powered (Table 2)\"\ncolumns: [\"meter_size\",\"accuracy_class\",\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q3\",\"q4\",\"q3_q1_ratio\"]\ncolumn_units: [null,null,\"m³/h\",\"m³/h\",\"m³/h\",\"m³/h\",null]\nrows: 25 rows as source.\n\nRow objects: {\"meter_size\":\"DN40\",\"accuracy_class\":1,...} for split rows; \"1 & 2\" as string for combined. Mixed types OK.\n\nRows:\nDN40, 1, 0.05, 0.08, 25, 31.25, 500\nDN40, 2, 0.025, 0.04, 25, 31.25, 1000\nDN50, 1, 0.08, 0.128, 40, 50, 500\nDN50, 2, 0.04, 0.064, 40, 50, 1000\nDN65, \"1 & 2\", 0.063, 0.1008, 63, 78.75, 1000\nDN80, \"1 & 2\", 0.1, 0.16, 100, 125, 1000\nDN100, 1, 0.32, 0.512, 160, 200, 500\nDN100, 2, 0.16, 0.256, 160, 200, 1000\nDN125, 1, 0.32, 0.512, 160, 200, 500\nDN125, 2, 0.16, 0.256, 160, 200, 1000\nDN150, \"1 & 2\", 0.4, 0.64, 400, 500, 1000\nDN200, \"1 & 2\", 0.63, 1.008, 630, 787.5, 1000\nDN250, 1, 2, 3.2, 1000, 1250, 500\nDN250, 2, 1, 1.6, 1000, 1250, 1000\nDN300, 1, 3.2, 5.12, 1600, 2000, 500\nDN300, 2, 1.6, 2.56, 1600, 2000, 1000\nDN350, 1, 3.2, 5.12, 1600, 2000, 500\nDN350, 2, 1.6, 2.56, 1600, 2000, 1000\nDN400, \"1 & 2\", 5, 8, 2500, 3125, 500\nDN450, \"1 & 2\", 5, 8, 2500, 3125, 500\nDN500, 1, 8, 12.8, 4000, 5000, 500\nDN500, 2, 4, 6.4, 4000, 5000, 1000\nDN600, 1, 12.6, 20.16, 6300, 7875, 500\nDN600, 2, 6.3, 10.08, 6300, 7875, 1000\n\ndescription: \"Flow rates Q1–Q4 and ratio Q3/Q1 per meter size and accuracy class (Table 2, pages 3–4; table continues across pages). Q1 and Q2 are minimum values, Q3 and Q4 are maximum values; Q2/Q1 = 1.6, Q4/Q3 = 1.25; Q3/Q1 ≥ 40; Q3 and Q3/Q1 selected per OIML R49-1:2013 §4.1.\"\nfootnotes: [] — none numbered.\n\nmatrix_tables[1] (software):\nname: \"Approved software versions\"\ncolumns: [\"software_part_code\",\"version\",\"checksum\"]\ncolumn_units: [null,null,null]\nrows: 7.\n\ntype_level characteristics — final list:\n1. measuring_principle: {\"value\":\"Electromagnetic\",\"unit_symbol\":null,\"unit_id\":null}\n2. accuracy_class: {\"value\":\"1 and 2\",...} hmm — recommendation already has it; still fine to include. Use value \"1 and 2\"? Or [1,2]? Keep string \"1 and 2\". Eh — I'll skip accuracy_class in type_level since recommendation.accuracy_classes covers it? Table 1 explicitly lists it as a general characteristic. I'll include for fidelity: {\"value\": \"1 and 2\"}.\n3. environmental_class: {\"value\":\"O (installed outdoors)\"} — hmm. Decide: value \"O (installed outdoors)\". OK.\n4. electromagnetic_environment: \"E2\"\n5. mechanical_class: \"M1\"\n6. ambient_temperature_range: {min:-25,max:55}, \"°C\"\n7. water_temperature_class: \"T50\"\n8. water_temperature_range: {min:0.1,max:50}, \"°C\"\n9. maximum_admissible_pressure: 1.6, \"MPa\"\n10. maximum_admissible_pressure_bar: 16, \"bar\"\n11. orientation: \"All positions (horizontal, vertical, or diagonal)\" — keep original casing: \"All positions (Horizontal, vertical, or diagonal)\".\n12. reverse_flow: true — hmm; I'll use string \"intended to measure reverse flow\"? Value shape allows string. I'll use {\"value\": true}. Booleans are valid JSON; fine.\n13. checking_facilities: \"Type P (permanent) automatic checking facility\"\n14. q2_q1_ratio: 1.6\n15. q4_q3_ratio: 1.25\n16. minimum_q3_q1_ratio: 40\n17. documentation_folder: \"T11851-6\"? It's captured in test_reports. Skip.\n\nconfig_level entries as planned:\nA. flow_profile_sensitivity_class (axis \"bore type and meter size\"):\n - condition \"all sizes except full bore DN250 and larger\", value \"U0 and D0 (0 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream)\"\n - condition \"full bore DN250 and larger\", value \"U3 and D0 (3 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream)\"\nB. pressure_loss_class (axis \"bore type and meter size\"):\n - \"reduced bore, DN40–DN50\" → \"Δp 40\"\n - \"reduced bore, larger than DN50\" → \"Δp 63\"\n - \"virtual or full bore, DN40–DN50\" → \"Δp 10\"\n - \"virtual or full bore, DN65–DN200\" → \"Δp 16\"\n - \"virtual or full bore, DN250 and larger\" → \"Δp 10\"\nC. pressure_loss (axis same):\n - 0.40 bar; 0.63 bar; 0.10 bar; 0.16 bar; 0.10 bar\nD. power_supply_voltage (axis \"power supply type\"):\n - \"AC mains\" → {85,240} V\n - \"renewable energy power (DC)\" → {6,32} V\n - \"replaceable battery (2 cells)\" → 3.6 V\nE. power_supply_frequency (axis \"power supply type\"):\n - \"AC mains\" → {50,60} Hz\n\ntype_level battery:\n- battery_cell_count: 2\n- battery_operating_voltage_range: {2.9, 3.6} V\n\nHmm also \"DC powered\" wording: \"Renewable energy power (DC powered): 6 – 32 V\". condition: \"renewable energy power (DC powered)\".\n\nFootnotes:\n[{\"marker\":\"*\",\"text\":\"With X being 1 or 3 (standard or advanced), Y being 1, 2, 8 or 9 (integral/remote version, optionally sensor only) and Z being R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore) or F (full bore).\"}]\n\ntest_reports:\n[\n {\"id\":\"NMi-2254799-01\",\"date\":\"2020-08-14\",\"pages\":235,\"role\":\"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\":\"NMi-2254799-03\",\"date\":\"2020-09-30\",\"pages\":44,\"role\":\"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\":\"NMi-2254799-04\",\"date\":\"2020-12-24\",\"pages\":180,\"role\":\"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\":\"NMi-2564429-01\",\"date\":\"2021-08-02\",\"pages\":26,\"role\":\"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\":\"NMi-2496280-01\",\"date\":\"2021-08-26\",\"pages\":29,\"role\":\"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\":\"NMi-2496280-02\",\"date\":\"2021-11-23\",\"pages\":25,\"role\":\"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\":\"T11851-6\",\"role\":\"documentation_file\"}\n]\n\nrecommendation:\n{\"id\":\"R49-1\",\"edition\":2013,\"scheme\":\"A\",\"accuracy_classes\":[1,2]}\n\nHmm — id canonical: \"R49\" with part? The example canonicalizes \"OIML R 60\" → \"R60\". \"R 49-1 (2013)\" → \"R49-1\". I'll go with \"R49-1\".\n\nNow let me also double-check the power supply: \"AC mains: 85 –240 VAC @ 50/60 Hz\". VAC — voltage unit V (AC). power_supply_type \"AC\". I have config axis covering it. Also add type_level power_supply? Skip, config covers.\n\nAlso \"(operating range: 2,9 - 3,6 V)\" → battery_operating_voltage_range {min 2.9, max 3.6} V. Good.\n\nNow assemble the JSON carefully. Watch decimal commas: 0,05→0.05 etc. All handled.\n\nOne more consideration: characteristics.type_level key labels canonical snake_case:\n- measuring_principle\n- accuracy_class\n- environmental_class\n- electromagnetic_environment\n- mechanical_class\n- ambient_temperature_range\n- water_temperature_class\n- water_temperature_range\n- maximum_admissible_pressure (MPa)\n- maximum_admissible_pressure_bar (bar)\n- orientation\n- reverse_flow\n- checking_facilities\n- q2_q1_ratio (fixed minimum? note says \"the ratio Q2/Q1 = 1,6\" — it's the actual design ratio; the Q1/Q2 listed are minimum values meaning Q2 ≥ 1.6×Q1... Actually \"Values mentioned for Q1 and Q2 are minimum values and the ratio Q2/Q1 = 1,6.\" Hmm, that's odd but I'll record q2_q1_ratio: 1.6.)\n- q4_q3_ratio: 1.25\n- minimum_q3_q1_ratio: 40\n\nFor value objects, include unit_id: null and footnote_markers only when present. To reduce bloat, I'll include \"unit_id\": null consistently in type_level and config entries; model_level values per example shape {\"model\",\"value\"} — keep minimal plus footnote_markers when present (none).\n\nFor models[] entries attributes: {\"nominal_size_dn\": 40, \"accuracy_class\": 1}.\n\nLet me now also decide about DN400 \"1 & 2\" row ratio 500 for both classes — in model_level both DN400 c1 and c2 get 500. Yes.\n\nWriting JSON now. It'll be long. Ensure valid JSON: no trailing commas, proper escaping. Use \"Δp\" Unicode fine. \"m³/h\" Unicode fine. \"°C\" fine.\n\nModel id naming: \"DN40 class 1\". In matrix rows accuracy_class numeric 1/2 or string \"1 & 2\".\n\nDouble-check DN65: 0,063 / 0,1008 → 0.063 / 0.1008. Ratio: 63/0.063 = 1000 ✓.\n\nDN200: 630/0.63 = 1000 ✓. Q2=1.008=0.63×1.6 ✓.\n\nDN250 c1: Q1=2, ratio 1000/2=500 ✓; Q2=3.2 ✓. c2: Q1=1, ratio 1000 ✓; Q2=1.6 ✓.\n\nDN300 c1: 1600/3.2=500 ✓; Q2 5.12 ✓. c2: 1600/1.6=1000 ✓; 2.56 ✓.\n\nDN350 same as DN300 values ✓.\n\nDN500 c1: 4000/8=500 ✓, Q2 12.8 ✓. c2: 4000/4=1000 ✓, Q2 6.4 ✓.\n\nDN600 c1: 6300/12.6=500 ✓, Q2 20.16 ✓. c2: 6300/6.3=1000 ✓, Q2 10.08 ✓.\n\nGreat.\n\nNow the final JSON. Order keys roughly per schema: certificate, issuing_authority, applicants, manufacturers, certified_type, model_family, characteristics, matrix_tables, recommendation, test_reports, footnotes.\n\nConfig entry shape decision (final): {\"condition\": \"...\", \"value\": <raw>, \"unit_symbol\": <sym|null>, \"unit_id\": null}. Consistent with rule 5's {condition, value, unit_symbol}. Add footnote_markers when applicable (none).\n\nmodel_level attribute entry: {\"attribute\": \"q1\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"DN40 class 1\", \"value\": 0.05}, ...]}. unit_id not in example; skip.\n\ntype_level value objects: {\"value\": ..., \"unit_symbol\": ..., \"unit_id\": null} (+ footnote_markers when present).\n\nLength check — 30 models × (1 entry in models + 5 values) ≈ fine.\n\nLet me write it.",
